\viewkind4\uc1\pard\fi-270\li270\sl202\slmult0\cf1\ul\b\f0\fs24\'b6 Verse 1\ulnone\b0 
\par 1.\cf0    Praise thou the Lord, O my soul, \tab 
\par       now give Him praise!
\par \pard\li270\sl190\slmult0\qj His praise continues until my death!
\par While I the pathways of this earth I'm treading,
\par \pard\li270\sl190\slmult0\cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par \pard\li270\sl190\slmult0\qj God shall be praised with all within me.
\par My soul and my flesh He did give to me
\par and waits my praises from the morn till eve.
\par Hallelujah, Hallelujah.
\par 
\par \pard\fi-270\li270\sl190\slmult0\qj\cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 2\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par   2.   Happy, yes happy, are they that forever
\par \pard\li225\sl190\slmult0     Whose help the Lord God of Jacob is
\par \pard\li180\sl190\slmult0\qj     who hath created the earth and heaven,
\par \pard\li180\sl190\slmult0    the sea and all that there in is.
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6   Verse\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par Our God is ruler of the world,
\par \pard\li270\sl190\slmult0\cf1 truth's banner He hath e'er un-furl'd\cf0 
\par  Hallelujah, Hallelujah.
\par \tab 
\par \pard\fi-270\li270\sl190\slmult0\cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 3\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par \pard\fi-270\li270\sl190\slmult0\qj   3.  Praise Him O, ye people, the name most glorious
\par \pard\li270\sl190\slmult0\qj   Of Him who reigns the Almighty king!
\par   All should then unite in one holy chorus,
\par  in God, the Hymn of Joy to Him bring.
\par \pard\li270\sl190\slmult0\cf1\ul\b\'b6  Verse\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par \pard\li270\sl190\slmult0\qj O Zion come with the Heavenly host.
\par   praise to the father, son and Holy Ghost
\par \pard\li180\sl190\slmult0     Hallelujah, Hallelujah.
\par \pard\f1 
\par \cf1\ul\b\f2 
\par }

